> API and interpretation

The solver uses strict positive residuals/excesses rather than silently
discarding values below1e-12. Self-loops own valid residual pairs but keep zero
flow; parallel and antiparallel inputs keep separate identities. Every positive
residual/excess update must make finite representable progress, otherwise the
call fails explicitly. This is checked floating arithmetic, so a numerical
flow/cut certificate remains appropriate. Counts include final cut scans, and
exclude validation, allocation and callback-free container internals; they are
not wall-clock measurements.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [A new approach to the maximum-flow problem, Goldberg and Tarjan|https://doi.org/10.1145/48014.61051]

